### Tested versions

v4.7.stable.arch_linux [5b4e0cb0f]

### System information

Godot v4.7.stable (5b4e0cb0f) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 26 Jun 2026 07:16:33 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7600 (RADV NAVI33) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 31.10 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)

### Issue description

Using a custom `ShaderSky`, the radiance cubemap is correctly updated when one of the shader's uniforms is changed.

However, this does not happen when it's a _global_ uniform.

It happens both in the editor and in the running game.

### Steps to reproduce

Use the following sky shader:

```glsl
shader_type sky;

global uniform vec3 sky_color: source_color;
uniform vec3 ground_color: source_color;

void sky() {
	if (EYEDIR.y >= 0.0) {
		COLOR = sky_color;
	} else {
		COLOR = ground_color;
	}
}
```

When changing the `ground_color` from black to green, the scene's lighting is correctly updated:

<img width="1104" height="923" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ffd6925-6745-48b8-a8a6-0eef0f429800" />

But when changing `sky_color` to red through Project Settings, the scene's lighting is not affected:

<img width="1105" height="926" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f047f018-9faa-48a1-986c-0844f40e4fdc" />

Triggering an update by modifying `ground_color` shows the correct result:

<img width="1109" height="926" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13dff151-5201-491c-934e-310bf54523d8" />

